       "reasoning": "The user wants me to complete a function that checks if a string of brackets is correctly bracketed. This is a classic balanced parentheses problem.\n\nThe approach is straightforward:\n1. Use a counter to track the balance of brackets\n2. For each \"(\", increment the counter\n3. For each \")\", decrement the counter\n4. If the counter ever goes negative, return False (closing bracket without matching opening)\n5. At the end, return True if counter is 0 (all opening brackets matched)\n\nLet me write the complete solution.",
